<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bosnia-Herzegovina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bosnia-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a> is a region in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>, ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> for centuries. It was occupied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> in 1878 and formally annexed in 1908, a move that heightened Balkan tensions. Its predominantly rural economy and the assassination of Archduke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archduke-franz-ferdinand-of-austria">Franz Ferdinand</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarajevo">Sarajevo</a> in 1914 tied it to the fate of the Austro-Hungarian Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bosnia-herzegovina.jpg" alt="Bosnia-Herzegovina" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mladen Kolobarić · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Bosnia_and_Herzegovina.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
